{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1276","t":"Hi Victoryong,\n\nThank you for this. I was looking at a few different ways to do this and your rules look great. I have attached 8 examples. If you get a chance can you tell me what you think.\n\nThank you very much for your time.","a":"Tirnanog","d":"","n":"#1276","p":52,"im":["a722e5430286f862623b105a2a503004d11758cf"],"m":1276},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1277","t":"If anyone gets a chance could you tell me if the attached would be considered a Valid setup? mohsin360 and victoryong, Thank you for helping me. The process is captivating.","a":"Tirnanog","d":"","n":"#1277","p":52,"im":["a0078e32b112c17fd5fd2303222cf4d9010d7616"],"m":1277},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1278","t":"Hi Tirnanog, Your zone drawing is good to me, here are variation. Giving you options to choose from.\n\nCheers\n\nTirnanog wrote: Hi Victoryong,\n\nThank you for this. I was looking at a few different ways to do this and your rules look great. I have attached 8 examples. If you get a chance can you tell me what you think.\n\nThank you very much for your time.","a":"victoryong","d":"","n":"#1278","p":52,"im":["a16354f09480b88821becfb7b40993842f90495d"],"m":1278},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1279","t":"Thanks. I plan to get some practice in over the weekend, I'll try a lot of each to see what fits. Thanks again. I hope you have a great weekend.","a":"Tirnanog","d":"","n":"#1279","p":52,"im":[],"m":1279},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1280","t":"Just some more practice.","a":"Tirnanog","d":"","n":"#1280","p":52,"im":["4a3ed36a019b9147fbc6711d04027a6feed235cc","56a3e2dcd9ad3e2af19965377fcab9c379d39946","a56fbad0cbbb40d2316f5e5daa0d7556faf1574e"],"m":1280},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1281","t":"RBD Home","a":"AlvaroA26","d":"","n":"#1281","p":52,"im":["82876f46c758bd9952ccac24bf53f6f6134cbf85"],"m":1281},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1282","t":"I'm going to keep an eye on Gbp/Cad D1 looks like it will be coming up area of supply and make a nice drop. I found a few areas of DBD, RBD, etc. I'm sure there is more that I missed.","a":"AlvaroA26","d":"","n":"#1282","p":52,"im":["66916ebf7836f65b92f3d218907465907fef6030"],"m":1282},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1283","t":"Just looking for DBR and RBD. I have tried to take the extreme turning points, I'm not too sure if the levels in between at classified as RBR, DBD's","a":"cedge","d":"","n":"#1283","p":52,"im":["cc3c7708222b69e83198d79f39e7bf38b919fcb6"],"m":1283},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1284","t":"My goal is to find clear and reactive areas. Checks are rejections, \"x\"s are engulfs.","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1284","p":52,"im":["d896a2f83237b06de96c54bd12f5480bcdd13254"],"m":1284},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1285","t":"","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1285","p":52,"im":["fbf76bafd9b37f9ed707b3984ecaea8bce85f52e"],"m":1285},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1286","t":"I look for decisions to engulf something important and then watch what happens when price comes back to these DPs.","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1286","p":52,"im":["937ffe199de466b8d003842d44ffc8df1a26f61c"],"m":1286},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1287","t":"","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1287","p":52,"im":["43bd1697525bf866cef79cdf1ed9cf4da2a14a4a"],"m":1287},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1288","t":"","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1288","p":52,"im":["e4dd29550a9c84e177fe608d2345740f237c3abd"],"m":1288},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1289","t":"I think filled rectangles are less confusing.","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1289","p":52,"im":["152929f1be30768a5a30986b0b62849e58c18436"],"m":1289},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1290","t":"","a":"karlo","d":"","n":"#1290","p":52,"im":["a872f6032cf7ef9d95a07725971d79a7b7daa39c"],"m":1290},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1291","t":"Ifmyante wrote: This is quite a bit better.\n\nDid you notice how if one is ignored, it can stop price from coming back through again?\n\nHi MR IF Please answer this quastion! tnx sir.","a":"ofshen","d":"","n":"#1291","p":52,"im":[],"m":1291},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1292","t":"Ok, I started doing my homework. This is a first set of my HW. I focused on FTB and marked the reaction. Comments are welcome.\n\nNOTE: I do not marked every RBD, DBR, RBR or DBD because the chart would be very messy.","a":"deenius","d":"","n":"#1292","p":52,"im":["7de698838b2acf56c461d9f49757a9ecbc4462dd","ec6f1f2f55ddda3077177baa78ff59376efa16c1","4b141c03df27b7640521d27112c7dd529619a765","157d3c3dfabceabba92b3ed99681843cd6405f29","85c103694ac279021703e65946e42cff6b443153"],"m":1292},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1293","t":"Set number 2. Feel free to comment","a":"deenius","d":"","n":"#1293","p":52,"im":["755803f042c76ce2b562b7935e48fb587a4c1dae","6d447b45d09d615ca64c8079c0ed3dbb9073b598","b83419e09f4723fbc1028c3e6adc9db9edc44bfd","3fcadcc42bbd63522135533b7b139c425ff37fdf","ea95c4820579b1b724f23a0ff91f08dbf85ce55e"],"m":1293},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1294","t":"Set number 3. This is end for today","a":"deenius","d":"","n":"#1294","p":52,"im":["6fa677727e9add9b6a251580b5132807a8ecda22","793b52a0eaf145159d62fb42ae1ca95ed3b933f0","22ca9a22d632c8414c675a132995435b2871a58b","356b40163a86c4e6b8ae3ba642380e58ca28e300","3703b9135394e9f7fd39aaf1fe09aa159377b7df"],"m":1294},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1295","t":"Last set of charts. Could someone tell me if I'm doing my S/D levels in correct way? Thank you!","a":"deenius","d":"","n":"#1295","p":52,"im":["af18ef6d22ad4a8741a960d80b7537bb195374ef","802848734fc9c7f0d1b2120df3ef3f8f1ba1eb43","cc2e5a80bfb94bcc9b487b6661ddffe09e60664e","a5de4569bd05463d8b163008b4b33e2acdd081c6","2025301743c2a999c758c95ed3b45a0ae7d692e1"],"m":1295},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1296","t":"Hi Deenius,\n\nYes you are. However try to incorporate the sequences of h-l-hh-hl-hh-ll-lh-ll or (hh-hl-lh-ll) etc... even if it's only in your minds eye. Now go back over the charts you posted and look at the X areas. You will find that often a good demand for instance is one that is a higher low that either made a hh or is part of the base where the downtrend sequence shifted giving you the lowest low that is also often a qm zone.\n\nHope this helps,","a":"pucci","d":"","n":"#1296","p":52,"im":[],"m":1296},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1297","t":"Hi Pucci. Sorry for the stupid question...But WHEN do you consider an important DBR RBD no more important.?? In other words, you look for an engulf, consumption,spiked. Or shall we consider an important RBD DBR ALWAYS important?? Thank you..","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1297","p":52,"im":[],"m":1297},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1298","t":"Homework on Rally Base Drop and Drop Base Rally.","a":"prosenjitghosh","d":"","n":"#1298","p":52,"im":["ebaa30f69b54ad488b188c6f2a768296ada552b7"],"m":1298},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1299","t":"SO.........I completely looked skipped over this homework (not on purpose). Time to backtrack, here is partial HM for CAPS (still working on the others). Doing each TF on every pair. Any comments are welcome/encouraged. I know i didn't get them all but i couldn't figure out a way to show them all without the charts being unreadable.\n\nHopefully im on the right track","a":"Nehru82T","d":"","n":"#1299","p":52,"im":["61746e6a6163ce87b03c03db12a8666984abeb56","89de35c0807c4153ac1417ae83b30bdce5067e1d","ac8c5f57281a2fb4aa1a442a6a6ec4fa9d31841c","86ed4f73de121339584d0e179cc68a48ae757b32","2438f6e8b75276e1d3ca802bf2cdd30f124b2789"],"m":1299},{"id":"dbrrbd_p52_1300","t":"Gday All\n\nJust a small pic to check I'm doin this correctly...If someone who knows whats what could have a squiz over this for me and lemmie know I'd really appreciate it.\n\nCheers\n\nGypsy","a":"Gypsy","d":"","n":"#1300","p":52,"im":["e4416214ab513d545f0e91a91da0b9fc36cb37c1"],"m":1300}],"images":[{"k":"a722e5430286f862623b105a2a503004d11758cf","t":"assets/thumbs/a722e5430286f862623b105a2a503004d11758cf.webp","f":"assets/images/a722e5430286f862623b105a2a503004d11758cf.png","w":1473,"h":793,"b":34535,"o":"a722e5430286f862623b105a2a503004d11758cf.png","p":52,"pid":"dbrrbd_p52_1276"},{"k":"a0078e32b112c17fd5fd2303222cf4d9010d7616","t":"assets/thumbs/a0078e32b112c17fd5fd2303222cf4d9010d7616.webp","f":"assets/images/a0078e32b112c17fd5fd2303222cf4d9010d7616.png","w":1261,"h":825,"b":28177,"o":"a0078e32b112c17fd5fd2303222cf4d9010d7616.pn